From 7d40d6cd4c42e4004b1427f97ef697c2c6e36f1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moosylog <moosylog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:54:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lighting: persist brightness, background and the effects'
 on-brightness

The output brightness and the background were never stored, so a board
always booted at full brightness with its compiled background, and the
on/off switch a host sets through SetState (the output mode) was not
stored either. Turning effects off stores their value as 0, so after a
restart RgbTog brought them back at the compiled brightness.

- Storage: LightingOutputState (brightness and background) and
  LightingEffectsOnValue (the effects' last brightness above 0), each
  stored only when it differs, with readers for boot.
- SetState and settled lighting keys store the output mode, brightness
  and background; extension writes store the on-brightness.
- StandardLightingEngine::with_output_brightness, to boot at it.
- Tests: the records survive reopening storage; SetState and turning
  effects off reach storage (fails without the change).
